 +## A Hermes kanban ticket created with `--parent <open ticket>` can be neither claimed nor completed while that parent is open — `claim_rejected parents_not_done`, and `complete` answers the misleading "unknown id or terminal state" (2026-09-13, orchestrator, debate-tiers S03)
 +Seven finding tickets created with `--parent t_f14b0ca0` (V's slice ticket, open by design until V's veto) sat in `todo`; `promote --force` moved them to `ready` but `claim`/`complete` still refused, and the only error text that named the cause was in `show`'s event log (`claim_rejected {'reason': 'parents_not_done'}`). **Rule:** a parent on this board is a DEPENDENCY, not a folder. Link finding and node tickets under the node that produced or consumes them (`link <node> <ticket>` — a closed node satisfies), never under the slice ticket; if one was created with the slice as parent, `unlink <slice> <ticket>` first, then `complete`. Read `show <ticket>` (text) for the event log before retrying a refused transition — the JSON `status` alone does not explain a refusal.
