 +## A packet that freezes line anchors must freeze the HEADER too — "a Revision N line under the title" moves every anchor below it (2026-09-13, orchestrator, debate-tiers S03 ARCH-FIX p3)
 +The ARCH-FIX p3 packet required both "PLAN §1 :98-362 keeps its line count" (BUILD packets were written against those anchors) and "a `Revision 3` line under the title". Any line added above :98 moves S1; the seat resolved it by compressing the Revision 2 block by exactly the lines Revision 3 added. **Rule:** when a packet freezes line anchors, say what happens to the header (a fixed-height header region, or the revision note appended at the END of the file), or anchor by content (`**S1.`, a heading text) and let seats add lines freely. Related law from the same pass: every checker prints its denominator ("0 of N seen, N counted thus") and is validated on known-GOOD input before its verdict is quoted — two passes, two unvalidated checkers, both silent where they were incomplete.
