 +## Launch a fleet seat DETACHED (`nohup setsid … & disown`), never inside a harness-tracked background Bash task (2026-09-13, orchestrator, debate-tiers S03 BUILD launch)
 +The Bash tool's `timeout` caps at 600 000 ms and `run_in_background` does not document an exemption; a Codex BUILD seat runs 30–90 min. Two seats were launched as harness tasks, noticed at ~40 s, stopped and relaunched detached — cheap at 40 s, catastrophic at minute 10 (a seat killed mid-tool-call leaves partial edits and needs `codex exec resume`). **Rule:** the launcher `.sh` writes its pid file and `exec`s the CLI; **this Mac has NO `setsid`** (`nohup setsid …` dies with "setsid: No such file or directory" and leaves the stale pid file in place) — the orchestrator starts it from python, `subprocess.Popen(["zsh", launcher], stdout=log, stderr=STDOUT, stdin=DEVNULL, start_new_session=True)`, which puts the seat in its own session so the harness shell's exit cannot reach it; verifies the pid with `ps -o etime,command -p`, and watches the LOG (Monitor on the log or the watchdog), never the harness task. `TaskStop` on a harness-tracked launch kills the seat's process group.
