 +## A new pnpm workspace package links only AFTER its package.json exists AND the root manifest depends on it — an "install first, once" instruction cannot link a package a later step creates (2026-09-13, orchestrator, debate-tiers S03 BUILD-C1)
 +The BUILD-S03-C1 packet said "run your ONE `pnpm install` FIRST, before any test" to keep the install away from the sibling seat's vitest runs. The seat did; the package did not exist yet, so nothing was linked, and every root-level suite importing `@debateai/model-config` stayed BROKEN at collection. Root suites resolve a workspace package through the ROOT `package.json` (`"@debateai/<name>": "workspace:*"`, one line per package — `node_modules/@debateai/` is exactly that list), not through `pnpm-workspace.yaml`'s glob, which only discovers. **Rule:** a step that creates a workspace package (a) creates its `package.json`, (b) adds the root `workspace:*` dependency, then (c) runs `pnpm install` — in that order, and the packet says so; the lockfile and the root manifest are that cluster's writes. A packet that constrains WHEN an install may run must state what must already exist when it runs.
